    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i tried running it in isolation but it's still super inconsistent. sometimes it's a timeout, sometimes it's a weird dependency error, sometimes it actually says it passed but the artifacts are missing. it's like the environment is just changing under our feet. any specific ways to log or trace the environment state during the build so i can actually see what's happening when it glitches?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Enable detailed logging at the environment state level by injecting custom checks right before and after your flaky stage to capture variable values, cache hashes, and network connection timings. Consider capturing full screenshots or terminal logs of the run's beginning and end artifacts to visually confirm discrepancies between successful and failed builds. If standard Jenkins logs aren't enough, you might need to leverage an external observability tool like Datadog or Splunk to correlate build timing with broader infrastructure events.",
      "source": "target",
